By and large, this will be true.  It isn't so much gaining levels
willy-nilly, it's gaining levels _and descending_ that will get you in
trouble.  It helps to do the Mines first, as there is a plentiful supply
of armor off dwarves there.

Also note that mostly, armor will be a bigger factor than weaponry in
the early game, just so you aren't nickeled and dimed to death by the
low-level critters who do 1d3 or 1d4.  (You won't likely get to negative
AC, but once you're around AC0/AC1, those same low-level critters won't
be hitting you much anymore.)

